## 3. How Ichigo Plays: Behavioral Profile & Tactical Loop

Across 11,859 recorded decisions, Ichigo distributes its actions evenly across **Buffs (`W`, 32.2%)**, **Specials (`S`, 29.1%)**, and **Standard Attacks (`D`, 29.1%)**, using **Guards (`A`, 8.0%)** sparingly for high-value reads and suffering **Forced Stun Recovery (`IDLE`, 1.6%)** less than once every four matches.

### Action & Stance Distribution Matrix

| Primary Action | Total Uses | Share | `J` Stance | `K` Stance | `I` Stance | `L` Stance | `NONE` | Dominant Signatures |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **`W` (Buff / Utility)** | 3,824 | **32.2%** | 69 (1.8%) | **1,522 (39.8%)** | **2,010 (52.6%)** | 223 (5.8%) | 0 | `W+I` & `W+K` (92.4% of all `W`) |
| **`S` (Special Moves)** | 3,455 | **29.1%** | 445 (12.9%) | 337 (9.8%) | **1,195 (34.6%)** | **1,478 (42.8%)** | 0 | `S+L` & `S+I` (77.4% of all `S`) |
| **`D` (Standard Attacks)** | 3,448 | **29.1%** | **1,482 (43.0%)** | 445 (12.9%) | 814 (23.6%) | 707 (20.5%) | 0 | `D+J` workhorse poke (43.0% of `D`) |
| **`A` (Guard / Counter)** | 946 | **8.0%** | 60 (6.3%) | 177 (18.7%) | **540 (57.1%)** | 169 (17.9%) | 0 | `A+I` primary counter (57.1% of `A`) |
| **`IDLE` (Faint Stun)** | 186 | **1.6%** | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 186 | Forced recovery at 100 Faint |

### The Four-Stage Combat Loop

1. **Opening Buff-Stacking (`W+I` $\rightarrow$ `W+K`):**
Ichigo treats Rounds 1–2 as an investment window, launching **`W+I`** (2,010 total uses—the single most clicked button in its policy) and **`W+K`** (1,522 uses) at low execution charge (26%–55%). Rather than burning its starting 9 Chi immediately, Ichigo banks +1 Chi per turn up to 10–11 Chi while layering offensive/charge multipliers.
2. **High-Charge Special Detonation (`S+I` & `S+L`):**
Once buffs are active and Chi reaches 10–12, Ichigo unleashes high-charge `S`-moves (routinely **85%–100% execution charge**).
* **`S+I`** serves as the heavy armor-breaker: in optimal sequences (e.g., Match #109 vs. `Bullet Ant` Amazon or Match #118 vs. `Bullet Ant` V3), a Round 1–2 `W+I` + `W+K` setup feeds a Round 3 `S+I` at 91–99% charge that deletes **1,950 to 2,620 LP** in a single exchange.
* **`S+L`** (1,478 uses) is Ichigo's premier high-priority follow-up and round-closer, pairing lower Chi overhead with consistent 80%–100% charge accuracy to finish weakened targets.


3. **Chi & Faint Engine (`D+J` Neutral Control):**
When Chi drops below `S`-move thresholds or opponents turtle up, Ichigo pivots to **`D+J`** (1,482 uses, 43.0% of all `D` actions), backed by `D+I` and `D+L`. These strikes execute reliably at 65%–80% charge, regenerating **+1 to +3 Chi per round** while inflicting **+25 to +31 Faint** per hit—driving Ichigo's **28.8% Faint Infliction Rate** and creating free `DO_NOTHING` stun windows for uncontested `S+L` finishers.
4. **Emergency Faint-Cleansing (`W+L`) & Surgical Counters (`A+I`):**
* **Stun Prevention:** Ichigo monitors its own Faint gauge closely. When Faint accumulates into the 45–85 danger zone against aggressive rushdown, the policy triggers **`W+L`** (223 uses) to purge ~30–40 Faint immediately (on top of natural round decay), keeping full `IDLE` stun lockouts down to **1.6%**.
* **Selective Guarding:** Instead of passive blocking, Ichigo uses **`A+I`** (57.1% of all `A` actions) as a targeted read against high-charge enemy commitments, yielding a **22.6% A-Guard Counter Rate** and preserving Chi for counter-offensives.



---

## 4. Diagnostic Priorities for Next Training Cycle

* **Anti-Turtle Sequencing (`Beetle` AI):** Against `Beetle` opponents that chain `W+L` evasions (notably `001_005` X and `001_003` V3), Ichigo occasionally fires `S+L` into active evasion frames, draining Chi without LP return. Weighting `D+J` faint-stacking slightly higher when opponent evasion buffs are active will stabilize these 50%–57% matchups.
* **Early Rushdown Mitigation (`Bullet Ant` Amazon):** In losses against Master-tier Amazon (`14W – 16L`), greedy double-buff openings (`W+I` into `W+K`) occasionally leave Ichigo exposed to fast Round 1–2 `S+K`/`S+J` burst before its counter-offensive comes online. Incorporating an early `A+I` or `D+J` interrupt check on P2 openings against high-aggression profiles should flip the `Bullet Ant` Amazon split above 50%.

